# tests/app2.script (make test-app, tests/app.sh): the packs (and an old save) already in
# /APPS/XCOM as the player copied them; XCOM.HZA installed (the Installer keeps them),
# started from Programs > Games: the loading screen, the start menu, New Game, Beginner,
# a base placed, then saved in slot 2 (XCOMXT2.SAV in the app's folder).
1000 xcom\n
+0 wait install: asks:
+500 \n
+0 wait install:
+800 \n
# (the Desktop reads the new Programs list from the card: on the board's card a few
# seconds after the install)
+6000 {f10}
+400 {right}
# (the Programs menu checks each program on the card as it opens: about 2 s on the
# board's card, and the Games menu again)
+3000 {end}
+400 \n
+3000 \n
+0 wait xcom: start
+300 shot
+0 wait xcom: ready for input
+1000 shot
# the intro (if it plays) skipped by a key; the start menu: N, the difficulty (Enter),
# the base placed where the globe is (Enter, Enter), then Esc, Save, slot 2, a name
+1500 {space}
+6000 shot
+500 n
+5000 \n
+6000 \n
+6000 \n
+8000 shot
+500 {esc}
+3000 s
+3000 2
+3000 AP\n
+6000 shot
